    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** (73.35) headlining our lineup as the primary offensive engine. Facing a favorable matchup against Bassitt (4.91 xERA), **Junior Caminero** benefits from an elite xwOBA profile and a prime spot in the heart of the order, making him our strongest play. We are also capitalizing on high-ceiling opportunities for **Yordan Alvarez** (68.01) and **Caleb Durbin** (62.34). While **Yordan Alvarez** offers elite power against Kirby, **Caleb Durbin** remains a priority start specifically for his stolen base potential; he faces a favorable matchup against Chandler, and his ability to exploit a slow delivery gives him a significant boost in our scarcest category. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.57) also earns a strong start despite a platoon disadvantage, as his leadoff status and park factors keep his efficiency well above our 60-point threshold.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision was opting to bench **Chase Meidroth** (36.88), who fell just shy of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor.\" While **Chase Meidroth** offered a slight park advantage, the projection against Jobe was ultimately dampened by a high-skill SP matchup and a unfavorable spot in the batting order. We are maintaining a disciplined approach today, ensuring our active slots are occupied by high-efficiency bats rather than chasing marginal utility. Please note that **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Gary Sanchez** remain unavailable due to scheduled off-days or rest, limiting our flexibility for late-game adjustments. Managers should keep a close watch on **Dillon Dingler**, whose score of 56.65 is heavily bolstered by a platoon edge against Newcomb, though he carries the risk inherent in catching a tough lefty-heavy sequence.",
